EN WOODEN DOOR</code></td><td>Mon 2:26pm</td><td>Long Passage</td><td>(already open) THE WOODEN DOOR IS OPEN</td><td>still wins</td></tr><tr><td>102</td><td><code>WEST</code></td><td>Mon 2:28pm</td><td>Browns Study</td><td></td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>103</td><td><code>EXAMINE CLOSELY DRAWER</code></td><td>Mon 2:33pm</td><td>Browns Study</td><td>You closely examine the drawer. You see the drawer. Careful examination shows that the drawer has a false bottom.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>104</td><td><code>OPEN DRAWER</code></td><td>Mon 2:34pm</td><td>Browns Study</td><td>You open the drawer.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>105</td><td><code>EXAMINE CLOSELY FALSE BOTTOM</code></td><td>Mon 2:39pm</td><td>Browns Study</td><td>You closely examine the false bottom. You see a false bottom.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>106</td><td><code>OPEN FALSE BOTTOM</code></td><td>Mon 2:40pm</td><td>Browns Study</td><td>You open the false bottom.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>107</td><td><code>TAKE BANK BOOK</code></td><td>Mon 2:41pm</td><td>Browns Study</td><td>You take the bank account book.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>108</td><td><code>EXAMINE CLOSELY BANK BOOK</code></td><td>Mon 2:46pm</td><td>Browns Study</td><td>You closely examine the bank account book. While the balance in the account is very high the entries in the book indicate that substantial and regular withdrawals have been made recently. The account name is Mrs Brown.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>109</td><td><code>TAKE NOTE</code></td><td>Mon 2:47pm</td><td>Browns Study</td><td>You take the note.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>110</td><td><code>EXAMINE CLOSELY NOTE</code></td><td>Mon 2:52pm</td><td>Browns Study</td><td>You closely examine the note. The note reads &quot; I have some news of vital importance that I would like to discuss with you at your convenience. Signed. Tricia Fender. &quot;</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>111</td><td><code>OPEN WOODEN DOOR</code></td><td>Mon 2:52pm</td><td>Browns Study</td><