><td>Mon 4:45pm</td><td>Kings Cross Road</td><td></td><td>loses</td></tr></table></div><h3 id="walk12">12. Kings Cross Road to Slater Street by cab</h3><p><small>Steps 138-144, Mon 4:45pm to Mon 5:13pm.</small> HAIL CAB, climb in, SAY TO CABBIE &quot;GO TO SLATER STREET&quot;. Arrive 5:09pm, PAY 10D TO CABBIE, climb out and LOOK: there is a hidden door to the north.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="steps"><tr><th>Step</th><th>Type</th><th>Clock after</th><th>Where</th><th>The game replies</th><th>Without this line</th></tr><tr><td>138</td><td><code>HAIL CAB</code></td><td>Mon 4:46pm</td><td>Kings Cross Road</td><td>You hail the hansom cab. Inspector Lestrade says to the cabbie &quot; Go to Parliament Street. &quot;. The cabbie says to you &quot; Good afternoon guv&#x27;nor. &quot;.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>139</td><td><code>CLIMB INTO HANSOM CAB</code></td><td>Mon 4:48pm</td><td>Kings Cross Road</td><td>You climb into the hansom cab. Watson climbs into the hansom cab.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>140</td><td><code>SAY TO CABBIE &quot;GO TO SLATER STREET&quot;</code></td><td>Mon 4:49pm</td><td>Hansom Cab</td><td>You talk to the cabbie. You are in a hansom cab with Watson and the cabbie. Watson is carrying the daily chronicle. You are travelling the streets of London in a hansom cab, the sun shines through the windows onto your face.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>141</td><td><code>WAIT</code> &times;4 <small>(repeated until the reply shows &ldquo;Slater Street.&rdquo;)</small></td><td>Mon 5:09pm</td><td>Slater Street</td><td>You wait. You are in a hansom cab. The hansom cab is on Slater Street. To the north there is a hidden door. The cabbie says to you &quot; Right guv&#x27;nor that will be 10d. &quot;</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>142</td><td><code>PAY 10D TO CABBIE</code></td><td>Mon 5:10pm</td><td>Slater Street</td><td>You pay 10d. To the cabbie.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>143</td><td><code>CLIMB OUT</code></td><td>Mon 5:12pm</td><td>Slater Street</td><td>You climb out of the hansom cab. Watson climbs out of the hansom cab.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>144</td><td><code>LOOK</code></td><td>Mon 5:13pm</td><td>Slater Street</td><td>You are on Slater Street. To the north there is a hidden door. You can see Watson. Watson is carrying the daily chronicle.</td><td>loses</td></tr></table></div><h3 id="walk13">13. The opium den: the Major&#x27;s confession</h3><p><small>Steps 145-153, Mon 5:13pm to Tue 12:03am.</small> WAIT (80 times) until 11:53pm. While you wait the Major arrives by cab, does not pay and goes north through the hidden door; the cabbie shouts at him. WEAR the china man&#x27;s disguise to pass the narrow hidden door, go NORTH into the opium den and TAKE OFF the disguise: the Major confesses. WEAR it again, SOUTH, and SAY TO LESTRADE &quot;MAJOR PERCIVAL FFOULKES VISITED OPIUM DEN&quot;; Lestrade lets the Major go. TAKE OFF the disguise.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="steps"><tr><th>Step</th><th>Type</th><th>Clock after</th><th>Where</th><th>The game replies</th><th>Without this line</th></tr><tr><td>145</td><td><code>WAIT</code> &times;80 <small>(repeated until the reply shows &ldquo;11:5&rdquo;)</small></td><td>Mon 11:53pm</td><td>Slater Street</td><td>You wait. Major Percival Ffoulkes climbs out of the hansom cab. The cabbie, who now appears to be getting quite agitated, says &quot; What about me money guv&#x27;nor? &quot;. Major Percival Ffoulkes goes north. The cabbie shouts &quot; You bloody ...</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>146</td><td><code>WEAR CHINA MANS DISGUISE</code></td><td>Mon 11:54pm</td><td>in disguise</td><td>You wear the china mans disguise.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>147</td><td><code>LOOK</code></td><td>Mon 11:55pm</td><td>in disguise</td><td>The china man is on Slater Street. To the north there is a hidden door. The china man can see Watson. Watson is carrying the daily chronicle.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>148</td><td><code>NORTH</code></td><td>Mon 11:57pm</td><td>in disguise</td><td></td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>149</td><td><code>TAKE OFF CHINA MANS DISGUISE</code></td><td>Mon 11:58pm</td><td>Disgusting Opium Den</td><td>The china man takes off the china mans disguise. Major Percival Ffoulkes remarks to you &quot; Well Holmes you have found out my shameful secret, I am addicted to this vile opium and I confess, this is where I was last night. &quot;.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>150</td><td><code>WEAR CHINA MANS DISGUISE</code></td><td>Mon 11:59pm</td><td>in disguise</td><td>You wear the china mans disguise.</td><td>still wins</td></tr><tr><td>151</td><td><code>SOUTH</code></td><td>Tue 12:01am</td><td>in disguise</td><td></td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>152</td><td><code>SAY TO LESTRADE &quot;MAJOR PERCIVAL FFOULKES VISITED OPIUM DEN&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 12:02am</td><td>in disguise</td><td>The china man talks to Inspector Lestrade. Inspector Lestrade says &quot; Very good Holmes, I shall return to Leather head tomorrow to have another look Major Percival Ffoulkes enters.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>153</td><td><code>TAKE OFF CHINA MANS DISGUISE</code></td><td>Tue 12:03am</td><td>Slater Street</td><td>The china man takes off the china mans disguise. Inspector Lestrade says to Major Percival Ffoulkes &quot; You are free to go. &quot;. Inspector Lestrade hails the hansom cab. The cabbie says to Inspector Lestrade &quot; Hello guv&#x27;nor. &quot;.</td><td>loses</td></tr></table></div><h3 id="walk14">14. Slater Street to Kings Cross platform four (Tuesday 1:30am)</h3><p><small>Steps 154-165, Tue 12:03am to Tue 1:30am.</small> WAIT to 12:53am, HAIL CAB, SAY TO CABBIE &quot;GO TO KINGS CROSS ROAD&quot;, pay, and walk NORTHEAST up to platform four.</p><p><em>Note:</em> The first walkthrough warned that taking this cab at 12:20-12:45am leaves Lestrade stuck in a cab. That did not reproduce: waiting only until 12:3 instead of 12:5 (the cab is hailed at 12:34am) still wins.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="s