THWEST</code></td><td>Tue 12:09pm</td><td>Platform Two</td><td></td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>212</td><td><code>SOUTHWEST</code></td><td>Tue 12:11pm</td><td>Platform One</td><td></td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>213</td><td><code>SOUTHWEST</code></td><td>Tue 12:13pm</td><td>Kings Cross Station</td><td></td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>214</td><td><code>SOUTHWEST</code></td><td>Tue 12:15pm</td><td>Kings Cross Road</td><td></td><td>loses</td></tr></table></div><h3 id="walk19">19. Kings Cross Road to Portman Street by cab</h3><p><small>Steps 215-221, Tue 12:15pm to Tue 12:57pm.</small> WAIT to 12:30pm, HAIL CAB, SAY TO CABBIE &quot;GO TO PORTMAN STREET&quot;. Arrive 12:54pm, pay, climb out.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="steps"><tr><th>Step</th><th>Type</th><th>Clock after</th><th>Where</th><th>The game replies</th><th>Without this line</th></tr><tr><td>215</td><td><code>WAIT</code> &times;3 <small>(repeated until the reply shows &ldquo;Tue 12:3&rdquo;)</small></td><td>Tue 12:30pm</td><td>Kings Cross Road</td><td>You wait.</td><td>still wins</td></tr><tr><td>216</td><td><code>HAIL CAB</code></td><td>Tue 12:31pm</td><td>Kings Cross Road</td><td>You hail the hansom cab. The cabbie says to you &quot; Hello guv&#x27;nor. &quot;.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>217</td><td><code>CLIMB INTO HANSOM CAB</code></td><td>Tue 12:33pm</td><td>Kings Cross Road</td><td>You climb into the hansom cab. Watson climbs into the hansom cab.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>218</td><td><code>SAY TO CABBIE &quot;GO TO PORTMAN STREET&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 12:34pm</td><td>Hansom Cab</td><td>You talk to the cabbie. You are in a hansom cab with Watson and the cabbie. Watson is carrying the daily chronicle. You are travelling the streets of London in a hansom cab, the sun shines through the windows onto your face.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>219</td><td><code>WAIT</code> &times;4 <small>(repeated until the reply shows &ldquo;tricias&rdquo;)</small></td><td>Tue 12:54pm</td><td>Portman Street</td><td>You wait. You are in a hansom cab. The hansom cab is in Portman Street. To the south there is tricias front door. The cabbie remarks to you &quot; Right guv&#x27;nor that will be 8d. &quot;</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>220</td><td><code>PAY 10D TO CABBIE</code></td><td>Tue 12:55pm</td><td>Portman Street</td><td>You pay 10d. To the cabbie. The cabbie pays 2d. To you.</td><td>still wins</td></tr><tr><td>221</td><td><code>CLIMB OUT</code></td><td>Tue 12:57pm</td><td>Portman Street</td><td>You climb out of the hansom cab. Watson climbs out of the hansom cab.</td><td>loses</td></tr></table></div><h3 id="walk20">20. Tricia Fender&#x27;s house</h3><p><small>Steps 222-237, Tue 12:57pm to Tue 1:37pm.</small> OPEN TRICIAS FRONT DOOR, south, OPEN THICK HEAVY DOOR, south into Tricias Lounge (1:03pm). The first SAY TO TRICIA FENDER gets an answer (it is really Mrs Jones); after that the person is called Mrs Jones and the next two get &quot;I SEE NO TRICIA FENDER&quot;. Then SAY TO MRS JONES &quot;TELL ME ABOUT YOUR ALIBI&quot; three times. OPEN WALL SAFE (15 minutes), EXAMINE CLOSELY the unfinished note and the folder (&quot;Top Secret. Military plans.&quot;). Back out to Portman Street.</p><p><em>Note:</em> Steps 226, 227 and 228 are the same line. Any one of them can be left out, but leaving only the first loses, so the extra lines matter even though two of them fail (checked). The bug entry on stale quotations describes how a failed SAY leaves its quotation behind; whether that is why the failing lines matter was not checked directly.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="steps"><tr><th>Step</th><th>Type</th><th>Clock after</th><th>Where</th><th>The game replies</th><th>Without this line</th></tr><tr><td>222</td><td><code>OPEN TRICIAS FRONT DOOR</code></td><td>Tue 12:58pm</td><td>Portman Street</td><td>You open tricias front door.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>223</td><td><code>SOUTH</code></td><td>Tue 1:00pm</td><td>Tricias Entrance Hall</td><td></td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>224</td><td><code>OPEN THICK HEAVY DOOR</code></td><td>Tue 1:01pm</td><td>Tricias Entrance Hall</td><td>You open the thick heavy door.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>225</td><td><code>SOUTH</code></td><td>Tue 1:03pm</td><td>Tricias Lounge</td><td></td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>226</td><td><code>SAY TO TRICIA FENDER &quot;TELL ME ABOUT BLOODSTAINED CLOTHES&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 1:04pm</td><td>Tricias Lounge</td><td>You talk to Tricia Fender. Mrs Jones says to you &quot; Oh my god, you found out, I am really Mrs Jones. Tricia was blackmailing Mrs Brown about something. I just could not let her hurt my friend like that so I planned to get rid of ...</td><td>still wins</td></tr><tr><td>227</td><td><code>SAY TO TRICIA FENDER &quot;TELL ME ABOUT BLOODSTAINED CLOTHES&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 1:04pm</td><td>Tricias Lounge</td><td>(no effect) I SEE NO TRICIA FENDER THAT YOU CAN TALK TO</td><td>still wins</td></tr><tr><td>228</td><td><code>SAY TO TRICIA FENDER &quot;TELL ME ABOUT BLOODSTAINED CLOTHES&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 1:04pm</td><td>Tricias Lounge</td><td>(no effect) I SEE NO TRICIA FENDER THAT YOU CAN TALK TO</td><td>still wins</td></tr><tr><td>229</td><td><code>SAY TO MRS JONES &quot;TELL ME ABOUT YOUR ALIBI&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 1:05pm</td><td>Tricias Lounge</td><td>You talk to Mrs Jones. Mrs Jones says to you &quot; Tricia was blackmailing Mrs Brown about something. I just could not let her hurt my friend like that so I planned to get rid of her. I had no idea that she had already killed poor ...</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>230</td><td><code>SAY TO MRS JONES &quot;TELL ME ABOUT YOUR ALIBI&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 1:06pm</td><td>Tricias Lounge</td><td>You talk to Mrs Jones. Mrs Jones says to you &quot; Tricia was blackmailing Mrs Brown about something. I just could not let her hurt my friend like that so I planned to get rid of her. I had no idea that she had already killed poor ...</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>231</td><td><code>SAY TO MRS JONES &quot;TELL ME ABOUT YOUR ALIBI&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 1:07pm</td><td>Tricias Lounge</td><td>You talk to Mrs Jones. Mrs Jones remarks to you &quot; Tricia was blackmailing Mrs Brown about something. I just could not let her hurt my friend like that so I planned to get rid of her. I had no idea that she had already killed poor ...</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>232</td><td><code>OPEN WALL SAFE</code></td><td>Tue 1:23pm</td><td>Tricias Lounge</td><td>You open the wall safe.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>233</td><td><code>EXAMINE CLOSELY UNFINISHED NOTE</code></td><td>Tue 1:28pm</td><td>Tricias Lounge</td><td>You closely examine the unfinished note. It is addressed to Mrs Brown and reads &quot; Meet me by the bridge at... &quot;.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>234</td><td><code>EXAMINE CLOSELY FOLDER</code></td><td>Tue 1:33pm</td><td>Tricias Lounge</td><td>You closely examine the folder. The folder is empty but the label reads &quot; Top Secret. Military plans. &quot;.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>235</td><td><code>NORTH</code></td><td>Tue 1:35pm</td><td>Tricias Entrance Hall</td><td></td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>236</td><td><code>OPEN TRICIAS FRONT DOOR</code></td><td>Tue 1:35pm</td><td>Tricias Entrance Hall</td><td>(already open) TRICIAS FRONT DOOR IS OPEN</td><td>still wins</td></tr><tr><td>237</td><td><code>NORTH</code></td><td>Tue 1:37pm</td><td>Portman Street</td><td></td><td>loses</td></tr></table></div><h3 id="walk21">21. Portman Street to Scotland Yard</h3><p><small>Steps 238-247, Tue 1:37pm to Tue 1:57pm.</small> HAIL CAB and climb in. SAY TO CABBIE &quot;GO TO PARLIAMENT STREET&quot; four times: the first two and the last only get &quot;You talk to the cabbie&quot;, and the cab sets off on the third (1:43pm). Arrive 1:54pm, pay, climb out and go EAST into Scotland Yard.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="steps"><tr><th>Step</th><th>Type</th><th>Clock after</th><th>Where</th><th>The game replies</th><th>Without this line</th></tr><tr><td>238</td><td><code>HAIL CAB</code></td><td>Tue 1:38pm</td><td>Portman Street</td><td>You hail the hansom cab. The cabbie says to you &quot; Hello guv&#x27;nor. &quot;.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>239</td><td><code>CLIMB INTO HANSOM CAB</code></td><td>Tue 1:40pm</td><td>Portman Street</td><td>You climb into the hansom cab. Watson climbs into the hansom cab.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>240</td><td><code>SAY TO CABBIE &quot;GO TO PARLIAMENT STREET&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 1:41pm</td><td>Portman Street</td><td>You talk to the cabbie.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>241</td><td><code>SAY TO CABBIE &quot;GO TO PARLIAMENT STREET&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 1:42pm</td><td>Portman Street</td><td>You talk to the cabbie.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>242</td><td><code>SAY TO CABBIE &quot;GO TO PARLIAMENT STREET&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 1:43pm</td><td>Hansom Cab</td><td>You talk to the cabbie. You are in a hansom cab with Watson and the cabbie. Watson is carrying the daily chronicle. You are travelling the streets of London in a hansom cab, the sun shines through the windows onto your face.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>243</td><td><code>SAY TO CABBIE &quot;GO TO PARLIAMENT STREET&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 1:44pm</td><td>Hansom Cab</td><td>You talk to the cabbie.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>244</td><td><code>WAIT</code> &times;2 <small>(repeated until the reply shows &ldquo;parliament&rdquo;)</small></td><td>Tue 1:54pm</td><td>Parliament Street</td><td>You wait. The cabbie replies &quot; Sorry guv&#x27;nor I cannot get there from&#x27;ere &quot;. You are in a hansom cab. The hansom cab is on Parliament Street. Visible exits are east. The cabbie says to you &quot; Right guv&#x27;nor that will be 4d. &quot;</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>245</td><td><code>PAY 10D TO CABBIE</code></td><td>Tue 1:55pm</td><td>Parliament Street</td><td>You pay 10d. To the cabbie. The cabbie pays 6d. To you.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>246</td><td><code>CLIMB OUT</code></td><td>Tue 1:57pm</td><td>Parliament Street</td><td>You climb out of the hansom cab. Watson climbs out of the hansom cab.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>247</td><td><code>EAST</code></td><td>Tue 1:57pm</td><td>Scotland Yard</td><td></td><td>loses</td></tr></table></div><h3 id="walk22">22. Scotland Yard: the statements</h3><p><small>Steps 248-255, Tue 1:57pm to Tue 2:07pm.</small> Two bare SAY TO LESTRADE lines and a TALK TO LESTRADE open the conversation, then SAY TO LESTRADE &quot;MRS BROWN KILLED HERSELF&quot; and &quot;MRS JONES KILLED TRICIA FENDER&quot; (he is delighted; Mrs Jones is led away). &quot;TRICIA FENDER HAD PLANS&quot; gets &quot;I do not see the importance of that&quot;; &quot;PHIPPS HAS PLANS&quot; and &quot;THE SALE LOCATION IS OLD MILL ROAD&quot; get &quot;I do not believe that you have the evidence&quot;.</p><p><em>Note:</em> PHIPPS HAS PLANS is not said again in this route; the sale location is said again at step 323.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="steps"><tr><th>Step</th><th>Type</th><th>Clock after</th><th>Where</th><th>The game replies</th><th>Without this line</th></tr><tr><td>248</td><td><code>SAY TO LESTRADE</code></td><td>Tue 2:00pm</td><td>Scotland Yard</td><td>You talk to Inspector Lestrade.</td><td>still wins</td></tr><tr><td>249</td><td><code>SAY TO LESTRADE</code></td><td>Tue 2:01pm</td><td>Scotland Yard</td><td>You talk to Inspector Lestrade.</td><td>still wins</td></tr><tr><td>250</td><td><code>TALK TO LESTRADE</code></td><td>Tue 2:02pm</td><td>Scotland Yard</td><td>You talk to Inspector Lestrade.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>251</td><td><code>SAY TO LESTRADE &quot;MRS BROWN KILLED HERSELF&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 2:03pm</td><td>Scotland Yard</td><td>You talk to Inspector Lestrade. Inspector Lestrade remarks &quot; So Mrs Brown killed herself, excellent Holmes, another brilliant</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>252</td><td><code>SAY TO LESTRADE &quot;MRS JONES KILLED TRICIA FENDER&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 2:04pm</td><td>Scotland Yard</td><td>You talk to Inspector Lestrade. Inspector Lestrade remarks &quot; Brilliant Holmes, I do not know how you do it. &quot;. He calls for a constable who leads the very distressed Mrs Jones out of the room into the depths of Scotland</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>253</td><td><code>SAY TO LESTRADE &quot;TRICIA FENDER HAD PLANS&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 2:05pm</td><td>Scotland Yard</td><td>You talk to Inspector Lestrade. Inspector Lestrade remarks &quot; I do not see the importance of that</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>254</td><td><code>SAY TO LESTRADE &quot;PHIPPS HAS PLANS&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 2:06pm</td><td>Scotland Yard</td><td>.&quot;. You talk to Inspector Lestrade. Inspector Lestrade says &quot; I do not believe that you have the evidence to prove that Basil Phipps has the plans &quot;.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>255</td><td><code>SAY TO LESTRADE &quot;THE SALE LOCATION IS OLD MILL ROAD&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 2:07pm</td><td>Scotland Yard</td><td>You talk to Inspector Lestrade. Inspector Lestrade says &quot; I do not believe that you have the evidence to prove that the sale location is the old mill road &quot;.</td><td>still wins</td></tr></table></div><h3 id="walk23">23. Scotland Yard to Basil&#x27;s front yard; wait for the window</h3><p><small>Steps 256-269, Tue 2:07pm to Tue 10:03pm.</small> WEST, HAIL CAB, SAY TO CABBIE &quot;GO TO CAMDEN STREET&quot; (arrive 2:18pm), pay, climb out, EAST into Basils Front Yard. WAIT and LOOK until &quot;Someone opens the window&quot; at 10:03pm.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="steps"><tr><th>Step</th><th>Type</th><th>Clock after</th><th>Where</th><th>The game replies</th><th>Without this line</th></tr><tr><td>256</td><td><code>WEST</code></td><td>Tue 2:09pm</td><td>Parliament Street</td><td></td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>257</td><td><code>HAIL CAB</code></td><td>Tue 2:10pm</td><td>Parliament Street</td><td>You hail the hansom cab. The cabbie remarks to you &quot; Good afternoon guv&#x27;nor. &quot;.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>258</td><td><code>CLIMB INTO HANSOM CAB</code></td><td>Tue 2:12pm</td><td>Parliament Street</td><td>You climb into the hansom cab. Watson climbs into the hansom cab.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>259</td><td><code>SAY TO CABBIE &quot;GO TO CAMDEN STREET&quot;</code></td><td>Tue 2:13pm</td><td>Hansom Cab</td><td>You talk to the cabbie. You are in a hansom cab with Watson and the cabbie. Watson is carrying the daily chronicle. You are travelling the streets of London in a hansom cab, the sun shines through the windows onto your face.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>260</td><td><code>WAIT</code> &times;1 <small>(repeated until the reply shows &ldquo;camden&rdquo;)</small></td><td>Tue 2:18pm</td><td>Camden Street</td><td>You wait. You are in a hansom cab. The hansom cab is in Camden Street. To the northeast there is the front door. Visible exits are east. The cabbie says to you &quot; Right guv&#x27;nor that will be 2d. &quot;</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>261</td><td><code>PAY 10D TO CABBIE</code></td><td>Tue 2:19pm</td><td>Camden Street</td><td>You pay 10d. To the cabbie. The cabbie pays 8d. To you.</td><td>still wins</td></tr><tr><td>262</td><td><code>CLIMB OUT</code></td><td>Tue 2:21pm</td><td>Camden Street</td><td>You climb out of the hansom cab. Watson climbs out of the hansom cab.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>263</td><td><code>LOOK</code></td><td>Tue 2:22pm</td><td>Camden Street</td><td>You are in Camden Street. To the northeast there is the front door. Visible exits are east. You can see Watson and a hansom cab. Watson is carrying the daily chronicle. In the hansom cab there is the cabbie.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>264</td><td><code>EAST</code></td><td>Tue 2:24pm</td><td>Basils Front Yard</td><td></td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>265</td><td><code>LOOK</code></td><td>Tue 2:25pm</td><td>Basils Front Yard</td><td>You are in Basils Front Yard. To the northeast there is the window. Visible exits are west. You can see Watson. Watson is carrying the daily chronicle.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>266</td><td><code>WAIT</code> &times;80 <small>(repeated until the reply shows &ldquo;Tue 09:4&rdquo;)</small></td><td>Tue 9:05pm</td><td>Basils Front Yard</td><td>You wait.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>267</td><td><code>WAIT</code> &times;7 <small>(repeated until the reply shows &ldquo;Tue 09:4&rdquo;)</small></td><td>Tue 9:40pm</td><td>Basils Front Yard</td><td>You wait.</td><td>loses</td></tr><tr><td>268</td><td><code>LOOK</code> &times;10 <small>(repeated until the reply shows &ldquo;Tue 09:5&rdquo;)</small></td><td>Tue 9:50pm</td><td>Basils Front Yard</td><td>You are in Basils Front Yard. To the northeast there is the window. Visible exits are west. You can see Watson. Watson is carrying the daily chronicle.</td><td>still wins</td></tr><tr><td>269</td><td><code>LOOK</code> &times;13 <small>(repeated until the reply shows &ldquo;Someone&rdquo;)</small></td><td>Tue 10:03pm</td><td>Basils Front Yard</td><td>You are in Basils Front Yard. To the northeast there is the window. Visible exits are west. You can see Watson. Watson is carrying the daily chronicle. Someone opens the window.</td><td>loses</td></tr></table></div><h3 id="walk24">24. Inside Basil&#x27;s house in disguise (Tuesday night)</h3><p><small>Steps 270-295, Tue 10:03pm to Tue 10:51pm.</small> WEAR the china man&#x27;s disguise, NORTHEAST through the window, through the oak door and the thick heavy door to Basils Library; TAKE the ripped coded note (step 277 mistypes it and gets &quot;WHAT ?&quot;), TAKE OFF the disguise to EXAMINE CLOSELY it. North-west to the passage, the plain door, the kitchen and back door to Basils Yard; EXAMINE CLOSELY the trash pile, TAKE and EXAMINE CLOSELY the torn coded note. WEAR the disguise again and retrace to the front yard (10:51pm); TAKE OFF.</p><p><em>Note:</em> Step 282 tries to open a door that is already open and can be left out.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="steps"><tr><th>Step</th><th>Type</t